+# Publication News and direct track sharing — 2026-10-18
+
+PUB07 adds a creator headline when publication is accepted. PUB08 supplies a share icon in the publication banner, News articles and published Free Race details. PUB09 opens the exact shared version directly in Free Race detail, without starting a race. PUB10 handles native/custom/web/legacy links with startup, race, navigation and account fences. G01/R01/Q01 retain normal racing, verification and bounded service work.
+
+Successful publication now writes one idempotent `track_published` News item for its creator in the existing publication transaction, including later accepted revisions. Friends retain the original shared first-publication fact; no per-friend inbox fan-out is added. Pending or failed publication does not produce an owner headline. Existing News feed reads and demand scheduling remain unchanged, including the three-read outline/feed check. Cleanup still obeys its original per-pass limit; an expired owner headline and its shared publication fact take separate budget units.
+
+The client also builds the creator's headline immediately from durable confirmed workflow receipts, including while local downloading is unfinished. Dismissing the acceptance banner leaves the article available. At most 30 recent local publication articles merge into the existing 100-item News window. Server rows replace local rows by immutable version on refresh and later pages; account changes clear the local projection. No News read/job is triggered by publication or an idle menu. Opening the existing newspaper retains its normal bounded refresh behavior.
+
+The newspaper uses its original printed layout and circuit outline, with a **Track published** category and an ink share icon. The acceptance banner and selected published-track hero also offer 52-unit share controls. Android opens the existing native chooser with the track name and link; desktop copies the same payload and presents a styled confirmation. Sharing the banner does not dismiss the unread acceptance. Original Race track actions remain ordinary five-lap starts.
+
+Published metadata now supplies `/t/{version_id}` links. The new public browser route reuses the exact metadata endpoint's publication, account, owner-hide and Studio-quarantine checks, escapes title/creator text and offers `beatmytrack://track/{version_id}`. It performs no track-document read or verification. Old `/v1/track-versions/{version_id}` API links remain supported by the client and Android filters. The game receives custom links, configured HTTPS app links and `--track-link=` launch arguments through the existing adapter, separately from challenges. Only the validated version identifier is resolved through the configured API; the incoming URL's host cannot redirect requests.
+
+Opening a link clears previous discovery filters, retains the acknowledged version and opens its Free Race detail. Later catalogue heads do not replace that explicit version. Choosing another track or closing detail releases the pin. Startup delays delivery; an active race queues the latest link until exit. Older replies cannot replace newer navigation, another account's view, or a newer link queued during racing. Existing immediate publication navigation, challenge URLs and challenge sharing remain.
+
+Checks completed with pinned Godot 4.7.2: new flow **39 headless / 39 Compatibility / 39 desktop Mobile**, existing News **62**, rendered original newspaper **334 Compatibility**, durable publication notification **54**, App **140**, project parser **886**, and import. Native captures show the [banner share icon](evidence/publication-news-share-2026-10-18/compatibility/publication-banner-share.png), [creator article](evidence/publication-news-share-2026-10-18/compatibility/publication-news.png) and [linked Free Race detail](evidence/publication-news-share-2026-10-18/compatibility/shared-free-race-detail.png). These are disposable local fixtures, not live publication or phone evidence.
+
+Backend SQLite checks pass: News/link tests **26 passed, 2 skipped**, current publication/private-route regression **21 passed, 2 skipped**, and a final three-test link smoke after import cleanup. PostgreSQL variants were deselected; PostgreSQL/concurrency validation is not claimed. Existing Starlette/SQLite reflection/test-report warnings remain. News expectations now explicitly include the creator's one private headline while retaining no friend fan-out, idempotency, exact provenance, query bounds and per-pass retention assertions.
+
+The actual Java adapter passes **22 host checks** with small Android/Godot platform doubles: accepted/rejected links, one-time pending-intent delivery, track chooser payload and unchanged challenge sharing. Its source also compiles against the actual Android 36 SDK and pinned Godot AAR with Java release 17; no APK is exported. Inspection of that pinned GodotActivity confirms that `onNewIntent` calls `setIntent`, matching the retained warm-link polling adapter. The same pure manifest generator used by Android export is tested for custom, HTTPS track, legacy API and original challenge filters.
+
+An older full Free Race layout suite still fails its populated-score fixture: it reports a missing TrackSafety action and then dereferences that missing control. A separate current-source runtime with only this task's App/TrackBrowser changes reversed reproduces the exact failure. That suite is not claimed passing; its source/assertions were not changed. The new actual linked-track view retains visible High scores, Rate, Report/block, favorite, close, share and Race controls, as captured. The comparison shares local asset/import junctions, has no Git source identity and never restores files into the working project.
+
+Initial attempts are retained: a News pagination indentation error was corrected; a concurrent editor coroutine transition temporarily prevented app parsing and was corrected by that work; the new test originally checked a moving share control before its tween settled and now waits for the real transition. An editor-only export-plugin instance was replaced with a shared pure manifest generator. A quarantine fixture now creates the required case/audit rows. Earlier backend expectations were updated for the requested creator headline rather than weakening fan-out or retention guarantees. Direct SDK-jar compilation printed an access exception despite returning zero, so it was not counted as passed; the final compile uses an exact workspace copy of the SDK jar and checks both diagnostics and generated classes.
+
+Actual commands, hashes, logs, scope and [task-only patch](evidence/publication-news-share-2026-10-18/task-only.patch) are in [report.json](evidence/publication-news-share-2026-10-18/report.json). Concurrent editor/loading/checkpoint/Rivalry work is preserved. No canonical physics/rules/content version or migration changes are part of this task.
+
+Updated game and backend/link-route rollout remain. Direct HTTPS app opening also requires the existing `BMT_CHALLENGE_LINK_HOST` and matching package/signing-certificate association documented in `docs/CHALLENGES.md`; these settings were not activated or fabricated. The custom-scheme button remains available on the browser preview. Real chooser behavior, installed-app association and owner/device acceptance remain. No phone attachment check/device test, APK/export/install, live publication, backend mutation or deployment was performed.
